    description: "Pluggable DefUseExtractor for Rust (~500-800 lines). Handles Simple+Moderate patterns: let bindings, tuple/struct destructuring, if-let/match, reassignment, field writes, for loops, closures (conservative capture), return. ? operator handled structurally (CFG creates dual edges, extractor treats Ok binding as simple let). Builds on existing rust.py scope analysis. See ADR-0017 §1c."  # 1408
